  "description": "The proposed design seeks to undertake a number of small external alterations to both improve the building energy performance for greater long term sustainability, and improve the health & safety for maintenance personnel to the high level roof:\n\n1.\tCreation of a new rear dormer to the roof;\n2.\tRefurbishment of the existing windows (excluding the ground floor shopfront glazing to No. 6 Kenrick Place) with new painted timber framed double glazed units;\n3.\tRefurbishment of the glazed roof lantern with a new metal frame with double glazed units;\n4.\tAlteration of an existing window opening to allow the installation of a painted timber double doorset with accompanying Juliet balcony railing;   \n5.\tThe installation of two new rooflights to the west facing pitched roof;\n6.\tApplication of frosted manifestation film to a small number of west elevation windowpanes to mitigate solar glare;\n7.\tImprove the current poor health & safety maintenance access at roof level with a new access door, and the installation of  safety balustrading and safety access walkway;\n",
